GNU grep sources for Debian
===========================

GNU grep's official distribution point is a CVS server, but upstream
helpfully supplies a git repository as well.  That is what we use.
It can be found at <git://git.sv.gnu.org/grep>.

With each new upstream version, debian/generated.list is regenerated
from upstream's .cvsignore files.  The commands to do this follow:

	# commit id of the release
	cid=$(git rev-parse upstream/master)

	git ls-tree -r "$cid" |
	grep cvsignore |
	awk '{ print $4 }' |
	while read filename
	do
		git show "$cid:$filename" |
		sed "s,^,${filename%.cvsignore},"
	done > debian/generated.list
